---
title: Field notes
eleventyNavigation:
  key: Field notes
  order: 2.5
---

{# Capture the CSS content as a Nunjucks variable and feed it through to the cssmin filter to minify it #}
{% set css %}
{% include "styles/archive.css" %}
{% include "styles/field-notes.css" %}
{% endset %}
<style>
	{{css | cssmin | safe}}
</style>

<p>These short and unpolished TIL snippets are written mostly as a reference for future me so I can find them again later when I need them. They are inspired by the pocket notebooks I carry with me when I'm on the move to jot down any stray thoughts or when I'm learning something new.</p>

{% set fieldNotes = collections.fieldNotes or [] %}

{# Hidden until the script below runs, since the filters do nothing without JS #}
<div class="archive__filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by tag" hidden>
	<button type="button" class="archive__filter" data-tag="" aria-pressed="true">All ({{ fieldNotes | length }})</button>
	{%- for tag in fieldNotes | usedTags %}
		<button type="button" class="archive__filter" data-tag="{{ tag.id }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ tag.title }} ({{ tag.count }})</button>
	{%- endfor %}
</div>

<ul class="field-notes__grid">
	{%- for note in fieldNotes | reverse %}
		<li class="archive__list-item" data-tags="{{ note.data.tags | join(' ') }}">
			<a href="{{ note.url }}" class="field-notes__card">
				<span class="field-notes__card-title">
					{{ note.data.title }}
					{% if note.data.draft %}
						<span aria-label="Draft">✍️</span>
					{% endif %}
				</span>
			</a>
		</li>
	{%- endfor %}
</ul>

<script>
	{% include "scripts/archive-filters.js" %}
</script>
